  "body": "Stacked on #1060 (tool import modes). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\nTools carry optional catalog facts: part number, vendor, coating, helix angle (deg) and notes.\n- `Tool.catalog: ToolCatalog` (new `camcraft_tools::catalog_fields`). Inert: no generator, check or post reads it; no golden moved.\n- `ToolDto` gets five additive keys, written only when stated, so tools without facts save byte for byte as before (no version step, old files load, older builds skip the keys). `.camproj` and `.camtools` share it.\n- `AddTool` / `ChangeTool` trim the text (blank = not stated) and refuse by tool name: helix outside 0..=90 or non-finite, part/vendor/coating over 80 chars, notes over 500, control characters. `Tool::is_sane` carries the same check so hand-edited files refuse by tool name too.\n- Tool editor: a collapsed \"Catalog\" header after Material group (open when any fact is stated; keeps the editor's height). Edits ride Apply/Add through the undoable commands, one undo step. The Body section is untouched (#1043).\n- MCP: `add_tool`'s `definition` takes the keys and `get_job` shows them. Editing an existing tool has no MCP tool at all: filed #1062. Setup sheet display: filed #1063.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/898-tool-catalog-fields.md`. #1060's Update/Replace still match by name; matching on part number is a behaviour change left for the maintainer.\n\n## Tested\nPinning: `crates/app/tests/tool_catalog_fields.rs` (project round-trip, library round-trip, no keys when empty and old JSON loads, one undo step and geometry unchanged, trimming, refusals by name, bad library helix), `catalog_fields::tests::normalizes_and_refuses`, ui `tool_catalog_rows::tests::the_draft_carries_the_facts_both_ways`.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/899-tool-import-modes` green on the final head (tools, motion, app, ui); clippy -D warnings clean on tools/app/ui/motion.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo GUI hand test of the new rows, no release-lane snapshot run (no PNG changed), no full batch tier.\n\nChangelog: Tools can store part number, vendor, coating, helix angle and notes (editor, .camproj, .camtools, MCP add_tool) (#898)\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #898\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
